Resume host clarifications from GNOME G7 part C (D57)

R78 points 1, 2, 4 and 5, adopted in D57.

1. SPEC-CONTROL D52.5: the app asks to resume only after the extension's
   status no longer reports a session for that tab. Before that the
   extension is still tearing the old session down and refuses the Start,
   which would spend the only ask.
2. auto-start-vectors.json meeting rows carry pageState "present", as real
   rows do; an absent page state is unknown and holds back a resume ask.
4. Dead spans after a fast reload: a documentChanged control frame in the
   stale-watchdog oracle, one case, one SPEC.md sentence. navigating retires
   every open span and opens a departing window whose declarations are
   retired; it closes on the next present or new documentGeneration. A new
   documentGeneration retires the spans declared up to the last frame that
   still reported the old one; a span declared after that stays armed. A
   retired span's PCM never re-arms it. Mutant tests cover each rule.
5. The resume Start example carries keepOnNavigation:true.

No extension code changes, so no version bump.

